  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hey there! I have a bit of a non-standard setup so this may be because of sensor placement or any number of other weird things I haven't considered, but VRChat seems to be the only game that this happens to me in.\n\nOccasionally when I am in VR and I move forward, when I stop pressing forward on the Rift's joystick, the game will continue to push me forward until I force myself backwards with the joystick, and even that it will resist several times as I try to get it to stop pushing me forward, sometimes with greater force than when I had originally attempted to stop moving.\n\nThere are times where all have to do is touch the joystick, not even pushing it to move forward and the game will still push my avatar forward. \n\nThere are also times where I move forward, stop pressing the joystick, remove my fingers from anything that could be sending an instruction to the game, and it still acts as if I am giving the \"move forward\" instruction through the joystick. \n\nThis ends up being pretty frustrating because it means whenever this bug shows up (and it is frequent) I have almost no control over my avatar standing still. \n\nThanks in advance for looking into this.\n\n- With Love, TheArchitect",
